## Enright-Pryce Suite

The purpose of this benchmark is to test explicit Runge-Kutta methods on the Enright-Pryce test suite, a collection of non-stiff ODE problems designed for testing numerical integrators.

```julia
using OrdinaryDiffEq, ParameterizedFunctions, ODEInterface,
      ODEInterfaceDiffEq, LSODA, Sundials, DiffEqDevTools,
      StaticArrays, OrdinaryDiffEqSIMDRK
using Plots
gr()
include(joinpath(@__DIR__, "..", "workprecision_table.jl"))

# Load the problems from the Enright-Pryce suite
include(joinpath(@__DIR__, "enright_pryce.jl"))

abstols = 1.0 ./ 10.0 .^ (6:13)
reltols = 1.0 ./ 10.0 .^ (3:10)
const ENRIGHT_PRYCE_ERROR_FLOOR = 1.0e-14
const ENRIGHT_PRYCE_RK_TAGS = [:ordinarydiffeq, :explicit_rk, :nonstiff]
const ENRIGHT_PRYCE_SIMD_RK_TAGS = [:ordinarydiffeq, :simd_rk, :explicit_rk, :nonstiff, :rhs_calls_unavailable]
```

Each sweep requests only the endpoint error with `error_estimates = [:final]` and
attaches solver metadata tags to the results. The table accompanying each existing
work-precision figure reports the best endpoint error, that point's timing,
right-hand-side calls, accepted steps, and the computed convergence rate over mean
accepted step sizes. The existing solvers are adaptive, so the fixed-step observed
order is unavailable. Rate calculations exclude errors at or below `1e-14`, the
tolerance used to construct each numerical endpoint reference; an em dash means the
grid did not resolve a rate or a counter is unavailable. Under RHS calls, the dash in
SIMD-RK rows means "RHS-call count not reported: SIMD invocation unit is ambiguous".

### SIMD Algorithms

```julia
simdrkalgs = [
    Dict(:alg=>MER5v2(), :tags=>ENRIGHT_PRYCE_SIMD_RK_TAGS),
    Dict(:alg=>MER6v2(), :tags=>ENRIGHT_PRYCE_SIMD_RK_TAGS),
    Dict(:alg=>RK6v4(), :tags=>ENRIGHT_PRYCE_SIMD_RK_TAGS)
]
```

### Low Order Setup

```julia
setups = [
    Dict(:alg=>Tsit5(), :tags=>ENRIGHT_PRYCE_RK_TAGS),
    Dict(:alg=>Vern6(), :tags=>ENRIGHT_PRYCE_RK_TAGS),
    Dict(:alg=>Vern7(), :tags=>ENRIGHT_PRYCE_RK_TAGS),
    Dict(:alg=>Vern9(), :tags=>ENRIGHT_PRYCE_RK_TAGS),
    simdrkalgs...
]
```

## Non-Stiff NA Problems

### NA1

```julia
prob = NA_PROBLEMS[1]
test_sol = solve(prob, Vern9(), abstol=1/10^14, reltol=1/10^14, save_everystep=false, dense=false)
wp = WorkPrecisionSet(prob, abstols, reltols, setups; appxsol=test_sol, error_estimates=[:final], save_everystep=false, numruns=100)
na1_wp = wp
print_work_table(wp, ENRIGHT_PRYCE_ERROR_FLOOR)
plot(wp; title="NA1")
```

