## Non-Stiff ND Problems

The ND suite uses `sqrt` in the RHS, which triggers a `StackOverflowError` via
`NaNMath.sqrt(::VectorizationBase.Vec)` when combined with the SIMD-RK stack.
Use the non-SIMD subset of `setups` for these problems.

```julia
setups_nd = [
    Dict(:alg=>Tsit5(), :tags=>ENRIGHT_PRYCE_RK_TAGS),
    Dict(:alg=>Vern6(), :tags=>ENRIGHT_PRYCE_RK_TAGS),
    Dict(:alg=>Vern7(), :tags=>ENRIGHT_PRYCE_RK_TAGS),
    Dict(:alg=>Vern9(), :tags=>ENRIGHT_PRYCE_RK_TAGS)
]
```

### ND1

```julia
prob = ND_PROBLEMS[1]
test_sol = solve(prob, Vern9(), abstol=1/10^14, reltol=1/10^14, save_everystep=false, dense=false)
wp = WorkPrecisionSet(prob, abstols, reltols, setups_nd; appxsol=test_sol, error_estimates=[:final], save_everystep=false, numruns=100)
print_work_table(wp, ENRIGHT_PRYCE_ERROR_FLOOR)
plot(wp; title="ND1")
```

### ND2

```julia
prob = ND_PROBLEMS[2]
test_sol = solve(prob, Vern9(), abstol=1/10^14, reltol=1/10^14, save_everystep=false, dense=false)
